__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/

# Run artifacts. Everything under outputs/ belongs to the run that made it, on
# the machine that made it.
#
# These were committed once, and the consequence was worse than clutter: a fresh
# clone arrived with ten strategy-library entries about somebody else's paper.
# The library exists to answer "has this question been asked before", and
# trials_for_family feeds the deflated Sharpe trial count -- so a shipped
# library makes a new fund inherit another research programme's trial budget
# and prior answers. The worked examples are kept, for reference, in
# examples/outputs/.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
!outputs/README.md

# Individual-stock-level data. Same reasoning as outputs/ above, plus a hard
# constraint: GitHub blocks any file over 100MB outright, and this data is
# expected to be far larger than the index-level workbooks already tracked
# in data/raw/. The loader code and its documented expected schema are
# tracked; the data itself lives only on the machine that has it.
# See data/raw/stocks/README.md.
data/raw/stocks/*
!data/raw/stocks/.gitkeep
!data/raw/stocks/README.md

# The master-universe drop folder (ros/data/master.py). Same reasoning as
# data/raw/stocks/ above -- a master CSV is exactly the kind of file that's
# too big for GitHub, and it was never gitignored here until this file
# almost went in unprotected. Never commit anything dropped in here.
data/raw/master/*
!data/raw/master/.gitkeep
!data/raw/master/README.md
